rity-boundary-analysis` @ `d099492`), plus the text of the corrections it should consider. Additive: three Markdown documents and one manifest generator under `evidence/pr37-independent-review-v1/`, nothing else — `git diff --name-only 52f682c HEAD` lists only that directory.\n\nIt deliberately does **not** touch #37's branch. That branch is unchanged at its four commits; #37 was not merged, approved, commented on, or modified by this review, and `main` was not pushed to.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**#37 is ready for an explicit merge decision.** Its gate figures reproduce independently at the final head, its evidence manifest verifies with its own recipe, its new test derives from `roadmap.json` rather than from a copied list, and its negative control fails as claimed when run in isolation at `52f682c`. Nothing in it weakens the security boundary, touches a production path, or changes a milestone state.\n\nSix findings, all corrections to text rather than to conclusions — one `incorrect`, two `unsupported`, three `confirmed with qualification`:\n\n| # | Class | Where | Issue |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | `incorrect` | `SECURITY_BOUNDARY.md:34` | attributes the classification rule engine to `psm/registry.py`, which contains no code (`grep -cE '^(def \\|class \\|    def )'` = **0**); the vocabulary is `psm/contract.py:36`, enforced in `Contract.problems()` at `:114` |\n| F2 | `unsupported` | `:287` | cited test id omits `RegistryRulesTest`, so it does not resolve: `exit 1` as written, `exit 0` qualified |\n| F3 | `unsupported` | `:110` | Safe-Mode power-button sequence and on-device path have no counterpart in the PR's own `FALSIFIER-SOURCE-EXTRACTS-20261122.md` |\n| F4 | `confirmed with qualification` | `:299`, `:327` | \"those five\" counts the roadmap's list (5), not the six artefacts in the sentence above it; a generated table row is described as a printed sentence |\n| F5 | `confirmed with qualification` | `VERIFICATION-…log` §10 | the recorded full-suite gate was run at `c118e67`; no run is recorded for the head `d099492` (reproduced here: `Ran 933 tests`, `OK (skipped=109)`, exit 0) |\n| F6 | `confirmed with qualification` | `:324`, §9 | \"no crypto library imported anywhere in them\" is true for cipher/MAC/KDF/signature/TLS (0 hits); `hashlib.sha256` is present in 10 `tools/` modules — the definition needs stating in the sentence |\n\nTwelve further candidate findings were investigated and **dropped**, each with the command that cleared it (§5 of the record) — including the \"ten interfaces\" count, the 14-name `psm/` enumeration, the 107-vs-109 skip figures, the roadmap's `notes`-only diff, `HASHES.txt` (13 records, 13 OK), and all four external emulator citations, which now check out against primary sources.\n\n## Files\n\n* `PR37-INDEPENDENT-REVIEW-20261122.md` — method, findings, the six review questions answered, reproduction with real exit codes, limits, readiness.\n* `CORRECTION-PROPOSAL-20261122.md` — C1–C8: exact before/after text for each finding, with the measurement beside it, and why the proposal lives here rather than on #37's branch (`main` does not contain the file #37 adds).\n* `HASHES.txt`, `gen_manifest.py` — integrity record in the same shape as #37's own, verifiable with the same predicate.\n\n## Gates run for this branch\n\n`TMPDIR=/tmp make check` → **exit 0**: `Ran 929 tests in 62.412s`, `OK (skipped=109)`, `PASSED: 165 checks, 0 failures`, `DOCS OK: 69 Markdown files, 34 make targets`, `CITATIONS OK: 258 commit reference(s) … across 11 documents`, `PRESENTATION OK: 6 figures and 5 blocks current, 13 status rows match roadmap.json`. `make docs-check` → exit 0. Manifest: 2 records, 2 OK. These are repository gates in this sandbox — not CI (this repository reports no checks), not an approval, and not evidence about PS5 hardware or Sony's system software.\n\n## Not done here\n\nNo merge, no approval, no comment on #37, no change to any milestone state, no edit to `tools/`, `boot/`, `kernel/`, `psm/` or `ci/`. 